# Mohandes Man design system

Follow `docs/DESIGN-SYSTEM.md`. Keep visual decisions on semantic tokens.

## Tokens

- Source of truth: `css/globals.css`.
- Style with semantic utilities (`bg-primary`, `text-muted-foreground`, `border-border`).
- Do not use raw brand palette classes (`bg-blue-500`, `text-green-600`, `border-gray-200`) in reusable UI.
- Retheme by changing `:root` (and later `.dark`) variables, not by editing dozens of components.
- Do not scatter `dark:` color overrides in primitives. Dark values exist on `.dark` for a future theme.

## Primitives

- `components/ui` contains generic primitives only.
- Do not put domain or layout UI in `components/ui`.
- Folder shape: `components/ui/<componentName>/<componentName>.tsx`.
- No `index.ts` barrels.

## Visual direction

- Minimal, premium, professional, Persian-first, RTL-first, mobile-first.
- Prefer whitespace, typography, and hierarchy over decoration.
- Restrained borders and shadows. Cards are light, not floating by default.
- Glassmorphism is allowed only for floating search, sticky navigation, overlays, hero treatments, and modal/sheet surfaces. It is not the default for cards, forms, sections, or buttons.
- Pill radius is for tags, chips, selected filters, and small badges.

## Accessibility and direction

- Keep keyboard behavior, `focus-visible`, disabled/invalid states, labels, and semantic HTML.
- Default interactive controls should meet a comfortable mobile touch target.
- Prefer logical CSS (`start`/`end`, `ps`/`pe`, `ms`/`me`).
- Nested `dir` is only for LTR islands such as codes, phone numbers, and OTP.

## shadcn

- shadcn may provide accessibility, behavior, and composition.
- Mohandes Man tokens control appearance.
- Do not install unnecessary UI dependencies or another complete UI framework.
- Do not blindly add every shadcn component.
- If the CLI generates a flat `components/ui/button.tsx` file, relocate it to `components/ui/button/button.tsx` and fix imports.
- Review generated source before keeping it.
